  "status_text": "In this six-switch puzzle, a guess that always says no gets 50 of the 64 settings right. Split the switches into two groups of three. Say yes if exactly one group is all on. A predictor can combine switches and pairs of switches by adding their values modulo two. None can beat 50. Give it a genuine interaction between the two groups, and its best score drops to 46. Lean checked the sharp bound behind both scores (L-lib-416).",
